      "difficulty_level": "H2",
      "difficulty_reason": "The author generalizes finite-branching tree reasoning to coalgebras over abstract locally finitely presentable categories. The proof constructs a coproduct coalgebra, proves its well-foundedness through the exact mono/intersection hypotheses, and uses finite generation plus well-foundedness to obtain the directed join of finitely generated-carrier subcoalgebras. The categorical construction remains a substantial author obligation fully retained here. Set/nominal/convex instances and initial-algebra applications are supporting context and are not separately counted.",
